<title>UK: Standard Chartered up after Warburg note.</title>
<headline>Standard Chartered up after Warburg note.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Standard Chartered Plc were up 18-1/2p at 730p following upbeat comments in a banking sector review from broker SBC Warburg, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Warburgs is just the latest house to highlight banking stocks,&quot; one dealer said. &quot;Standard Chartered has underformed many in the sector, so its just catching up a bit.&quot;</p>
<p>No one at SBC Warburg was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
